{"id": "vbx-3", "title": "Swift facade over the C ABI", "description": "## Bridge design\n\nWraps the C ABI in an `actor` so calls serialise while the real\nconcurrency stays inside Go.\n\n- envelope decoding, one error path\n- buffer ownership released via `defer` on every path\n- cancellation maps to `vbx_cancel`\n\n```swift\nlet info = try await engine.open(path: workspace)\nlet metrics = try await engine.waitForPhase2()\n```\n\n> A panic must never cross the boundary; it is recovered at the ABI edge.\n\nSee **ADR-001** for why the engine is reused rather than ported.\n", "status": "in_progress", "issue_type": "feature", "priority": 0, "created_at": "2026-05-04T09:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-08-10T12:00:00Z", "labels": ["engine", "swift"], "assignee": "michel", "estimated_minutes": 480, "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "vbx-3", "depends_on_id": "vbx-2", "type": "blocks"}]}
